{% comment %}
  Desktop header row, logo size and dark-mode plate. Owner, 2026-09-02:
  "the logo should be beside the search as it is creating a lot of shite space
  and please make it 33% larger. also in dark mode it should lose its white
  background."
{% endcomment %}
<style>
  /* ==========================================================================
     DESKTOP HEADER (>= 992px): logo beside the search, logo 33% larger.

     Measured on the preview at 1440px (run 113, HEADER-DESK): logo img
     [55,68,52,52], #_desktop_search [55,120,500,40], logo wrapper
     [55,68,688,52]. The first ancestor the logo and the search share is the
     INNER .page-width (.nav-menu > .page-width), which modern-skin sets
     display:block - so the logo block spans the row, the icon cluster
     (.header-user-selection) stacks UNDER it, and 636px to the logo's right
     is blank. The 688 is the cluster's max-content: theme.css gives the
     search input min-width:500px. (This section's nesting is not what its
     indentation suggests - line 183 below is a commented-out </div>, see
     NOTES round 12b - so the structure above was measured, not read.)

     The fix turns that inner .page-width into the row: logo | search ...
     toggle / account / cart. The cluster keeps modern-skin's own flex order
     (search first via order:-1 + margin-right:auto, then the rest) - nothing
     is moved in the DOM and nav.megamenu-header is a sibling further out.

     Nothing here reaches below 992px: the phone header is gridded by
     xg-features.css under (max-width: 991px) and carries four CI checks
     from round 12b. Every layout rule sits inside (min-width: 992px); only
     the dark-mode plate removal (last rule) applies at all widths.

     Specificity. This <style> renders in the body, after every linked sheet,
     so equal specificity would already win - the margins below are so the
     ordering is not load-bearing:
       - modern-skin `#header .header-top .nav-menu > .page-width` (1,3,0)
         display:block / flex:0 0 auto  ->  the same selector with
         `.site-header-inner` added, (1,4,0).
       - theme.css `.page-width::after` (0,1,1) clearfix would become a flex
         item and take a gap of its own at the row's end -> content:none at
         (1,4,1).
       - modern-skin `#header .header-user-selection` (1,1,0) width:100%
         -> `#header .header-top.site-header-inner .header-user-selection`
         (1,3,0).
       - modern-skin `#_desktop_search` (1,0,0) max-width:680 and theme.css
         `#header #_desktop_search` (2,0,0) -> `#header .header-top
         .header-user-selection #_desktop_search` (2,2,0).
       - logo height: modern-skin `#header .header__logo img { max-height:
         52px !important }` (1,1,1) plus this section's inline style attr
         (max-height from the editor's logo_max_height: 120 in the preview's
         served settings_data.json, 2026-09-02 - the 52 on screen is
         modern-skin's cap, not the setting) ->
         `#header .header-top .header__logo img` (1,2,1) !important: an
         important declaration outranks the non-important inline style, and
         (1,2,1) beats (1,1,1) among importants. The theme setting itself is
         untouched and still governs below 992px.
       - dark plate: xg-dark `html[data-xg-theme="dark"] #header
         .header__logo img` (1,2,2) -> the same with `.header-top` added,
         (1,3,2).
     ========================================================================== */
  @media (min-width: 992px) {
    #header .header-top.site-header-inner .nav-menu > .page-width {
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 22px;
      flex: 1 1 auto;
      width: 100%;
      max-width: none;
    }
    #header .header-top.site-header-inner .nav-menu > .page-width::after {
      content: none;
    }
    #header .header-top.site-header-inner .header-logo-section-img,
    #header .header-top.site-header-inner .header-logo-section {
      flex: 0 0 auto;
      width: auto;
      margin: 0;
      padding: 0;
    }
    #header .header-top.site-header-inner .header-user-selection {
      flex: 1 1 0%;
      width: auto;
    }
    /* Search grows beside the logo to a sensible cap; theme.css's
       min-width:500px on the input is the floor. */
    #header .header-top .header-user-selection #_desktop_search {
      flex: 1 1 auto;
      max-width: 640px;
    }
    /* 52px x 1.33 = 69px. max-height (not height) keeps the aspect ratio
       if the asset is ever swapped for a non-square one. */
    #header .header-top .header__logo img {
      max-height: 69px !important;
      height: auto;
      width: auto;
    }
  }

  /* DARK MODE: no white plate behind the logo (owner: "in dark mode it
     should lose its white background"). xg-dark.css paints it as a spread
     box-shadow + white background (rounds 5/9/13); the PNG's own baked
     white ground is made transparent by a separate asset step, so a bare
     logo does not leave a white square. All widths on purpose - the plate
     was all widths. */
  html[data-xg-theme="dark"] #header .header-top .header__logo img {
    background: transparent;
    box-shadow: none;
    border-radius: 0;
  }
  /* ==========================================================================
     LANGUAGE SWITCHER (EN | FR) - 2026-09-02.
     Sits beside the dark-mode toggle in both slots (desktop icon cluster,
     phone bar). Tokens only (modern-skin.css light, xg-dark.css dark), so
     dark mode re-paints it with no rule of its own. Visibility is decided in
     Liquid (localization.available_languages.size > 1), never here.
     ========================================================================== */
  .xg-lang__form {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-self: center;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .xg-lang {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    height: 34px;
    padding: 0 3px;
    border: 1px solid var(--xg-border);
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--xg-ink);
    font-family: var(--xg-font-body);
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    line-height: 1;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .xg-lang__cur,
  .xg-lang__btn {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    height: 26px;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0 8px;
    border: 0;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: transparent;
    font: inherit;
    color: var(--xg-muted);
  }
  .xg-lang__cur {
    color: var(--xg-ink);
    font-weight: 700;
    background: var(--xg-red-soft);
  }
  .xg-lang__btn {
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: color var(--xg-fast) var(--xg-ease);
  }
  .xg-lang__btn:hover { color: var(--xg-red); }
  .xg-lang__btn:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--xg-red);
    outline-offset: 2px;
  }
  .xg-lang__sep {
    padding: 0 1px;
    color: var(--xg-border);
  }
  .xg-lang__form[aria-busy="true"] .xg-lang { opacity: 0.6; }
  #header .header-user-selection .xg-lang__form { margin-right: 10px; }
  #header .mobile-width-right .xg-lang { height: 30px; padding: 0 2px; }
  #header .mobile-width-right .xg-lang__cur,
  #header .mobile-width-right .xg-lang__btn { height: 24px; padding: 0 6px; }
</style>
{% comment %}
  Language switcher (EN | FR), 2026-09-02. Rendered ONLY when the shop has
  more than one published language, so it stays invisible until the owner
  publishes French (Settings > Languages) - no template or settings change
  needed. Every language other than the current one is a real submit button
  (name="locale_code"), so the switch works without JavaScript; Shopify's
  localization form supplies form_type, _method and return_to itself. The
  small script at the end of this file only keeps the query string in
  return_to and guards a double submit. Labels: the current language is a
  plain span with aria-current; each button is labelled in its own language
  (WAI practice for language switchers) and carries a lang attribute.
{% endcomment %}
{%- capture xg_lang_items -%}
  {%- for xg_lang in localization.available_languages -%}
    {%- if xg_lang.iso_code == localization.language.iso_code -%}
      <span class="xg-lang__cur" lang="{{ xg_lang.iso_code }}" aria-current="true" title="{{ xg_lang.endonym_name | escape }}">{{ xg_lang.iso_code | upcase }}</span>
    {%- else -%}
      <button type="submit" class="xg-lang__btn" name="locale_code" value="{{ xg_lang.iso_code }}" lang="{{ xg_lang.iso_code }}" aria-label="{% case xg_lang.iso_code %}{% when 'fr' %}Passer au français{% when 'en' %}Switch to English{% else %}{{ xg_lang.endonym_name | escape }}{% endcase %}" title="{{ xg_lang.endonym_name | escape }}">{{ xg_lang.iso_code | upcase }}</button>
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- unless forloop.last -%}<span class="xg-lang__sep" aria-hidden="true">|</span>{%- endunless -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
{%- endcapture -%}
<div id="header" data-section-id="{{ section.id }}" data-section-type="header-section">
